WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.946
Hi, Nick, how are you?

2
00:00:02.946 --> 00:00:04.540
I am very well, thank you.

3
00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:05.670
How are you doing?

4
00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:06.893
You look fantastic.

5
00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:10.030
Well, that's very generous.

6
00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:11.830
I'll pass that right back at you.

7
00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:13.247
Oh, thank you.

8
00:00:13.247 --> 00:00:14.690
The pandemic has been good to you.

9
00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:15.880
You look stunning.

10
00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:19.510
And the last time we saw each other was also a party.

11
00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:22.980 line:15%
It was a long time ago, yeah, Megan and I

12
00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:27.260 line:15%
came to a party at your house in the Hollywood Hills.

13
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:30.490 line:15%
And it was the only time in my life

14
00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:33.555
I've been to an actual Toga party.

15
00:00:33.555 --> 00:00:35.040
I am not kidding.

16
00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:37.440
As Nick attests, I am that guy.

17
00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:41.080
I threw a major like 500 person

18
00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:43.730
animal house style Toga party.

19
00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:46.620
And you were with your wife.

20
00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:51.450
Megan Mullally is a goddess.

21
00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:55.650
I love her as Karen, obviously on Will and Grace.

22
00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:57.810
She changed the course of all of our lives

23
00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:01.780
and embodied a character that became so famous and iconic

24
00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:05.834
which is such a, not easy feat for an actor to do.

25
00:01:05.834 --> 00:01:10.030
Absolutely, and imagine what a lucky donkey

26
00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:13.230
you would feel like if every morning you wake up

27
00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:17.783
and she's laying there next to you, it's pretty crazy.

28
00:01:17.783 --> 00:01:21.650
And how did you woo this goddess?

29
00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:24.990
We met doing a play 21 years ago

30
00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:28.843
and I invited her on a date.

31
00:01:32.038 --> 00:01:32.871
I left her a message

32
00:01:32.871 --> 00:01:35.670
and turned out it was a bit of a dirty trick.

33
00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:38.260
The phone number that she had,

34
00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:39.330
and this used to be a thing,

35
00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:42.630
when you had to like especially for women

36
00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:46.613
that might be harassed by people.

37
00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:50.060
You would give a fake number.

38
00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:53.093
So on the cast list, she put her fax number.

39
00:01:54.138 --> 00:01:56.800
And so it turned out that I had left a message

40
00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:58.040
on her fax machine.

41
00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:00.770
And a couple of weeks later,

42
00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:03.650
she saw the light blinking on her fax machine

43
00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:04.797
and listened to it.

44
00:02:04.797 --> 00:02:07.790 line:15%
And so it scored me some points

45
00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:09.810 line:15%
and it also scored me some guilt points.

46
00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:11.080 line:15%
Cause then she felt bad

47
00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:13.810 line:15%
and she had to actually go out to dinner with me

48
00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:15.090
to make it up to me.

49
00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:17.760
And then the rest is history.

50
00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:20.073
And here we are on the Drew Barrymore show.

51
00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:21.010
(audience laughs)

52
00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:22.960
And that's not the only time

53
00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:25.100
that you kind of went for it.

54
00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:28.033
Didn't a post-it help you land another job as well?

55
00:02:29.137 --> 00:02:33.193
Yes, I was auditioning for a part on The Office

56
00:02:33.193 --> 00:02:37.220
and the creator of Parks and Rec was a writer on The Office.

57
00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:41.990
And I was auditioning for him and he really liked me

58
00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:45.110
and he wanted to cast me in the part, but I couldn't do it.

59
00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:47.060
So he wrote my name on a post-it

60
00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:49.850 line:15%
and put it on his computer monitor

61
00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:53.917 line:15%
to remind himself three years later when they said,

62
00:02:53.917 --> 00:02:58.010
"Hey Greg Daniels said, we want to do a show together,"

63
00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:00.250
which became Parks and Recreation.

64
00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:03.670
He said, "Ah-hah, I have this post-it.

65
00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:06.570
I want this guy Nick Offerman on the show."

66
00:03:06.570 --> 00:03:09.120
And it ended up working out thankfully.

67
00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:12.710
And for my wrap gift, he found the post-it

68
00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:14.990
and he had it framed and gave it to me.

69
00:03:14.990 --> 00:03:16.970
We have a picture of it.

70
00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:19.110
I went in to read for Poltergeist

71
00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:21.050
and I didn't get the part

72
00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:25.130
but I got to come back for ET and that's that.

73
00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:26.290
Timing is everything.

74
00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:28.140
Sometimes it's a better thing

75
00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:30.270
that something didn't work out.

76
00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:32.840
And it's great that you have evidence of that.

77
00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:34.720
And by the way, even your first gig

78
00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:37.560
in like 1996 was a little unorthodox.

79
00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:40.800
You were on a Nickelodeon show called KaBlam!

80
00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:43.470
Will you tell us about that character of yours?

81
00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:46.090
Yeah, I mean midriff shirts

82
00:03:46.090 --> 00:03:47.800
used to be contractual with me.

83
00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:50.267
That was my thing back in the 90s.

84
00:03:51.310 --> 00:03:54.820
My friend Greg Harrison made this show called KaBlam

85
00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:58.083
and he brought me to Los Angeles to play the bad guy.

86
00:03:59.658 --> 00:04:01.350
It was like a live action cartoon.

87
00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:05.010
So it was cartoon acting, even though we were real people

88
00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:07.820
but the sets looked like cartoons.

89
00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:11.100
And it was really fun and crazy

90
00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:14.300
and was an incredible introduction to Hollywood.

91
00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:16.960
I love that, and speaking of animated,

92
00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:19.250
you play a single dad named Beef

93
00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:21.450
on the animated series, The Great North.

94
00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:23.100
I'm so excited about this.

95
00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:24.890
What are we going to get into?

96
00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:27.427
Well, I'm the dad of this family.

97
00:04:27.427 --> 00:04:30.610
The cast is just bananas all-stars.

98
00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:34.410
Aparna Nancherla, Dulce Sloan, Megan Mullally,

99
00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:38.330
Jenny Slate, Will Forte, Paul Rust and on and on.

100
00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:40.500
The guest cast is just crazy.

101
00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:43.270
And so to get to play with all these people

102
00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:45.400
who just make me laugh constantly

103
00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:49.890
in a vessel through which we're just delivering medicine

104
00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:51.470
we're making people laugh,

105
00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:53.580
but it's also really good hearted.

106
00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:56.090
One of my son's is gay.

107
00:04:56.090 --> 00:04:59.760
There's all kinds of social issues being addressed.

108
00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:03.130
So we're subtly trying to help all of us

109
00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:06.760
be more decent through a funny cartoon.

110
00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:10.608
It's like really wholesome messaging with farts.

111
00:05:10.608 --> 00:05:11.441
(audience laughs)

112
00:05:11.441 --> 00:05:15.020
And we need that, comedy is medicine, it just is.

113
00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:16.522
And I live for it.

114
00:05:16.522 --> 00:05:19.105 line:15%
(upbeat music)

115
00:05:20.766 --> 00:05:22.637 line:15%
♪ Oh oh oh oh ♪

116
